# Topic Labeling Process

This document describes the topic labeling procedure used for the final BERTopic model in the master thesis analysis. It is included to make the interpretation process more transparent without sharing original Reddit post texts.

## Purpose

The topic labels were created to provide interpretable summaries of the thematic clusters identified by BERTopic. Because topic models produce statistical clusters rather than ready-made psychological categories, the final labels were developed through a combination of computational output inspection and researcher-led qualitative interpretation.

## Topic Information Used for Labeling

After fitting the final BERTopic model, topic-level information was exported and inspected. The labeling process was based on:

* topic IDs,
* topic sizes,
* the ten highest-ranked keywords per topic,
* the three posts with the highest topic probability scores per topic,
* topic probability information,
* and the broader thematic focus of each cluster.

This made it possible to consider both keyword-based topic representations and the contextual meaning of posts that were strongly assigned to each topic.

## Researcher-Led Initial Labels

The first topic labels were developed manually by the researcher. For each topic, the highest-ranked keywords and the highest-probability posts were reviewed to identify the main narrative focus of the cluster.

The aim was not to label topics based on isolated keywords alone, but to interpret what kind of abusive relationship narrative each cluster represented. Particular attention was given to whether a topic mainly concerned leaving, custody concerns, trauma bonding, self-blame, abuse recognition, coercive control, post-separation harassment, emotional manipulation, or recovery after abuse.

## AI-Assisted Label Suggestions

In a second step, ChatGPT was used to generate additional label suggestions based on the same topic-level information. This was used as an interpretive support tool only.

The AI-generated labels were compared with the researcher-generated labels. In some cases, AI-assisted suggestions helped refine the phrasing of a label or identify a broader thematic pattern. In other cases, the researcher-generated label was retained because it better reflected the contextual meaning of the topic.

## Final Label Selection

The final topic labels were selected through researcher-led synthesis. The final labels were based on:

* semantic fit with the topic keywords,
* fit with the highest-probability posts,
* distinctiveness from other topic labels,
* relevance to abusive relationship dynamics,
* clarity for readers,
* and consistency with the terminology used in the thesis.

The final decision for each label was made by the researcher. ChatGPT-generated suggestions were treated as supporting material and were not used as automatic labels.

## Final Topic Labels

| Topic | Final Label                                              |
| ----- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| -1    | Outlier / Unclassified Posts                             |
| 1     | Leaving Abusive Partners with Children and Custody Fears |
| 2     | Trauma Bonding, Self-Blame, and Relationship Violence    |
| 3     | Recognizing and Interpreting Abuse Dynamics              |
| 4     | Healing and Emotional Recovery After Leaving Abuse       |
| 5     | Post-Separation Harassment and Social Invalidation       |
| 6     | Guilt, Self-Blame, and Emotional Coercion                |
| 7     | Trauma Bonding and Early Recovery After Abuse            |
| 8     | Emotional Blackmail and Psychological Manipulation       |

Topic `-1` represents posts that BERTopic did not assign to a coherent thematic cluster. It was included for transparency but was not interpreted as one of the eight substantive topics.

## Use in Later Analyses

After the final labels were selected, they were integrated back into the BERTopic outputs. The labeled topic information was then used in the topic overview table, visualizations, topic similarity analyses, and topic-level sentiment and emotion analyses.

## Ethical Note

The repository does not include original Reddit post texts or direct quotations. This documentation therefore describes the labeling process at an aggregated level only. The final topic labels should be understood as interpretive summaries of model-generated clusters, not as fixed psychological categories or diagnostic classifications.

## AI Use Note

ChatGPT was used to support the topic labeling process by generating preliminary label suggestions and alternative phrasings. The final labels were reviewed, edited, and selected by the researcher, who remains responsible for the final interpretation.
